Z||000000||hyhy4u||07-15-2001||06:43 PM||||I was told i might have a wheel bearing going bad...bad vibration...how do you even begin to check to see if you do??...this is off a 87 GT Auto..||||reg||5
Z||000001||fierohoho||07-15-2001||07:53 PM||||I would start with the easiest, put the front tires on the back and the backs on the front and see if the vibration moves to the front.<P>If that makes a difference have all four wheels balanced.<P>Who told you it may be a wheel bearing and why do they think so?<P>------------------<BR>'84 SE 2.5l<BR>'85 Coupe 2.5l now getting a 3800<BR>'86 SE 2.5l||||reg||1
Z||000002||AutoXer||07-15-2001||08:47 PM||||Jack the back of your car up and see if the wheel moves in ways it isn't suposed to.||||reg||1
Z||000003||hyhy4u||07-15-2001||09:10 PM||||A couple things..first off i did rotate the tires about a half a week ago just to see with that..but the tires are almost new and i cant do a "regular" rotation of course cause its got the GT wheels on it(wider in the rear)..secondly i was told it was a rear bearing from one of the other formum members on a Post about a month ago...thirdly i have noticed one of the rear tires dosnt have any wheels balancer things on it..lol..is it that common for tires not to need one or did one fall off...thanks for any info you can give me...i just might take that tire in and get it balanced to see..i dont know..im lost!, lol||||reg||1
Z||000004||rogergarrison||07-15-2001||09:34 PM||||if a tire mounter is really good (ie -lines up the color dot on new tire with valve stem) its very possible. I have 2 tires with no weights and there balanced almost perfect. When I was racing, we could move the tire around on the rim to get it pretty good too, that way didnt have to worry about knocking them off with full body contact  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Phil||07-15-2001||09:57 PM||||You must have 88GT wheels on your 87 if the rims are different sizes.||||reg||1
Z||000006||V8Fiero||07-15-2001||10:09 PM||||I just take the top of the wheel as the car sits and rock the crap out of it. You WILL feel movement if there is any.<P>Had an 84 that had bad bearings. Could really tell by this method.<P>Hope it helps.<BR>Scott<P>------------------<BR>86 SE Gold<BR>86 GT Red <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/RedRavensig.JPG"> <BR>"Trying to change from V8Fiero to RedRavenGT"||||reg||1
Z||000007||hyhy4u||07-16-2001||12:57 PM||||I tried your little "shake the heck out of it method", lol, and the rear tires didnt move at all..when i went to the front it had some movement in it..is this just the rack and pinon moving around or what...and back to the whole original thing..how can i just go ahead and check the bearings??||||reg||1
Z||000008||84Bill||07-16-2001||03:23 PM||||Wheel bearings in the rear typicly make a loud whomp whomp whomp sound as the wheel turns. The fronts usually make the noise when you turn corners. ||||reg||1
Z||000009||Raydar||07-16-2001||03:38 PM||||I found a bad rear wheel bearing by putting the back of the car on jackstands, and running the engine in 1st gear. As the wheels turned, I could hear a roar coming from the bad bearing. <BR>If you do this, be sure to block your front wheels and be sure the jackstands are steady.<BR>It's best if you can support the lower control arms with a floor jack. Otherwise, you can "overextend" the CV joints.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000010||hyhy4u||07-16-2001||04:21 PM||||hmm..now that i think about it sometimes my car does make a noise when i turn corners....but the strange thing is like once every 1000 miles il have like a 3 mile trip that the car just dosnt vibrate at all and runs so smooth..and then the next time i drive it it shakes like nuts..and my rear wheels dont have any "play" in tehm so im guessing the front bearings are bad..now can i check them to see if there bad..or just replace them..remember im not huge on funds right now..<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000011||starfighter007@msn.com||07-16-2001||06:08 PM||||If they are bad they cost aprox $10.00 but you can first try repacking them with grease and see if that helps.||||reg||1
Z||000012||hyhy4u||07-16-2001||08:25 PM||||Okie dokie..i just talked to my dad and im gonna get the wheel balanced tommarow at his work...il tell ya guys teh results of that, then we can go from there i guess, lol, thanks for all the help so far!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
